-- title:
--   Non-toric 𝔪-torsion at p descends to level N₀
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0\ge 1$ and a prime $p$ with $p\nmid N_0$, a valuation subring $A$ of a fixed algebraic closure of $\mathbf Q$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$ (the predicate `LiesOverPrime`), a `LevelData` $\Lambda$ for $(N_0,p,A)$ — a section $\sigma_A$ of the base over $\operatorname{Spec}A$ compatible with the generic point, a scheme $X$ over `base p` with a relative group law, and bijections of $J_0(N_0)(\overline{\mathbf Q})=$ `JZero N₀` with the generic-fibre points and of the level-$N_0$ degree-zero class group over the residue field of $A$ with the points over the residue point — satisfying `IsJacobian` (abelian-scheme bundle, commutativity, additivity and Galois equivariance of both parametrisations, agreement of reduction, and realisation of the Hecke algebra by endomorphisms over the base), and an object $O$ of `JZeroNeronObjectAtP`: a smooth, separated, locally finite type, quasi-compact, surjective group scheme over `base p` with preconnected fibres, commutative group law, a Galois- and Hecke-equivariant parametrisation of `JZero (N₀ * p)` by its generic-fibre points, flat surjective multiplication by every $n>0$, proper generic fibre and toric data. Assume `HeckeInputsAll` and `HeckeOperatorsCommuteBar` at levels $N_0p$ and $N_0$, so that `JZero (N₀ * p)` and `JZero N₀` are modules over `HeckeAlg` $=\mathbf Z[X_\ell:\ell$ prime$]$ with $X_\ell$ acting by `heckeOperatorBar`. Then for every maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ of `HeckeAlg` containing $p$ but not `heckeGen` at $p$, and every $x$ in `O.finPts p` — the subgroup generated by the $p$-torsion classes whose associated point extends to a point over $A$ — which is annihilated by $\mathfrak m$ and does not lie in `O.toricPts p`, the $\mathfrak m$-torsion submodule `heckeTorsion (JZero N₀) 𝔪` is non-zero.
--
--   This is the transport of $\mathfrak m$-torsion from level $N_0p$ down to level $N_0$ for the same maximal ideal, in the case where the variable at $p$ is invertible modulo $\mathfrak m$ (classically $U_p\notin\mathfrak m$), the geometric heart of Ribet's level-lowering argument at a prime of multiplicative reduction. It is used in assembling the data that compares the toric and finite subgroups of the Néron model at $p$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_JZeroNeronObjectAtP_heckeTorsion_ne_bot_of_mem_finPts_of_not_mem_toricPts.lean

